# Changelog Modal Update Rules

When the user requests adding a changelog entry after a feature update:

1. **Add to the top** of the changelog array in `app/page.tsx` (newest first). Use incrementing `id` starting from 0 for the newest item, and shift existing items' `id` values accordingly.

2. **Format** for each entry:
   ```tsx
   {
     id: 0,           // 0 = newest, higher = older
     date: 'YYYY.MM.DD',
     title: 'Short title of the update',
     body: 'Brief 1-2 sentence description for end users.',
   },
   ```

3. **Body text** must be concise (1-2 sentences max). It is user-facing, not developer-facing.

4. **Update the localStorage version key** (`CHANGELOG_SEEN_KEY` value in the "Don't show again" button) to match today's date in `YYMMDD` format so returning users see the new entry.

5. **Update the version check** in the `useEffect` that compares `seen < 'YYMMDD'` to use the same new date string.

6. **Set `openChangelog` default** to `0` so the newest entry is expanded by default when the modal opens.
